      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Questions",
      "links": [],
      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Can we say that a kind of grammatical chasm exists between the form of the proposition and that of the question? Is there a kind of world, as it were, of the question, whose difference, verging on the suspicion of a kind of lack, sets it in perpetual opposition to that other world, that of the statement? [...] And when it comes to actions, are there those that one could designate as interrogative? And what about objects?",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Robert Morris: \"Professional Rules.\" Critical Inquiry, 23 (Winter 1997).",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Ben Vautier",
      "links": [],
      "level": 4
